German is taught in public schools in several Brazilian states, often by a single teacher working in isolation from the university. IVG Brasil wants to change that: bring these teachers closer to research, offer training linked to universities and give visibility to the work done in the classroom.

## What IVG Brasil offers teachers

- Continuing education in partnership with universities
- Teaching materials selected by level
- A space to share projects and classroom experiences
- A place in the Germanic Studies community, including the Rio 2030 Congress

Do you teach German in a public school? [Tell us](../contato/) where and how.

For teacher training courses, it is also worth knowing the work of the [Goethe-Institut](https://www.goethe.de/ins/br/pt/unt/eng/dos.html) and of the teachers' associations linked to [BraDLV](https://bradlv.com.br/pt/index.php).

## You study German. What next?

People who learn German at school have more paths than they imagine. With a Letras Alemão degree you can teach, translate books and series, work in culture and exchange, do research in Brazil or study in German-speaking countries.

- **Teacher:** teaching German in schools, language courses and universities.
- **Translation:** carrying books, films and documents from one language to the other.
- **Research:** studying literature, language and culture and publishing what you find.
- **Culture and exchange:** working at cultural institutes, publishers, museums and international programs.

Want to know where to study? See what [Germanic Studies and the Letras Alemão programs](../pesquisa/) are.
